**join amgen’s mission of serving patients**


at amgen, if you feel like you’re part of something bigger, it’s because you are. our shared mission—to serve patients living with serious illnesses—drives all that we do.


since 1980, we’ve helped pioneer the world of biotech in our fight against the world’s toughest diseases. with our focus on four therapeutic areas –oncology, inflammation, general medicine, and rare disease– we reach millions of patients each year. as a member of the amgen team, you’ll help make a lasting impact on the lives of patients as we research, manufacture, and deliver innovative medicines to help people live longer, fuller happier lives.


our award\-winning culture is collaborative, innovative, and science based. if you have a passion for challenges and the opportunities that lay within them, you’ll thrive as part of the amgen team. join us and transform the lives of patients while transforming your career.  





**specialist is business systems analyst**



**duties:** build and maintain product requirements for life cycle management as well as create and maintain prioritized user stories backlog in partnership with product owner and business teams; drive business requirements, functional design, prototyping, process design (including scenario design, flow mapping), testing, training, defining support procedures and supporting implementations; bring product capabilities to life by translating concepts and ideas to software features; continuously advance team and stakeholder adoption of scaled agile framework (safe); work closely in a client\-facing role with a cross\-functional team of dti platform and product stakeholders; influence the customer product experience by translating data into insights and business value; work with data engineers in automating and building integrations for seamless data flow to anaplan, tableau, and other reporting platforms; and handle end\-to\-end requirements for development work, and management of backlog including tracking dependencies, risks, and decisions. may telecommute.

 **requirements:** master’s degree (or foreign equivalent) in business analytics, information systems or related field \& 3 years of experience in the job offered or in an information systems\-related occupation. position requires 3 years of experience in the following:


agile and scaled agile framework (safe) including agile scrum and safe environments with cross\-functional teams;


software development lifecycles and agile product delivery;


coverage and pricing intelligence in the biopharma, pharmaceutical, and healthcare domain;


developing advanced dashboards and reports using tools including tableau and power bi;


system development life cycle (sdlc), including requirements gathering, functional specification development, testing (uat, regression),and deployment and hyper care;


devops, ci/cd \& agile tooling including ci/cd pipelines and devops practices: jira, github, gitlab, confluence, and bitbucket;


management of agile ceremonies and story backlogs for multiple products;


creating and executing test plans, test cases, test scripts, and requirements traceability matrices (rtm);


quality assurance tools including zephyr;


design and execution of data pipelines and analytical models using databricks, and etl frameworks;


end\-to\-end involvement in data lifecycle: ingestion, transformation, storage, and access control;


microsoft project, smartsheet, servicenow, excel, and powerpoint for program tracking, reporting, change request lifecycle, and stakeholder presentations;


analyzing, customizing, and maintaining models in anaplan to support enterprise performance management, scenario planning, and budgeting processes;


python, r, and sql for data manipulation, statistical analysis, and automation;


data wrangling libraries, machine learning techniques, and jupyter notebooks; and


modern cloud\-based data technologies, including aws s3, aws ec2, and aws redshift.

 **contact:** interested candidates please apply via https://careers.amgen.com/en/search\-jobs and search for job \# r\-248213\.



job type: full time position. the annual salary range for this position in the u.s. is $138,674\.00 to $143,472\.00 per year. also, this position offers stock, retirement, medical, life and disability insurance and eligibility for an annual bonus or for sales roles, other incentive compensation. for more details visit https://careers.amgen.com/life\-at\-amgen/benefits/

 **what you can expect of us**


as we work to develop treatments that take care of others, we also work to care for your professional and personal growth and well\-being. from our competitive benefits to our collaborative culture, we’ll support your journey every step of the way.


the expected annual salary range for this role in the u.s. (excluding puerto rico) is posted. actual salary will vary based on several factors including but not limited to, relevant skills, experience, and qualifications.


in addition to the base salary, amgen offers a total rewards plan, based on eligibility, comprising of health and welfare plans for staff and eligible dependents, financial plans with opportunities to save towards retirement or other goals, work/life balance, and career development opportunities that may include:


* a comprehensive employee benefits package, including a retirement and savings plan with generous company contributions, group medical, dental and vision coverage, life and disability insurance, and flexible spending accounts
* a discretionary annual bonus program, or for field sales representatives, a sales\-based incentive plan
* stock\-based long\-term incentives
* award\-winning time\-off plans
* flexible work models, including remote and hybrid work arrangements, where possible
 **and make a lasting impact with the amgen team.**

